        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Can you run out of Life tokens, and still <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z7DhzeTp9SQ\">create life</a> on a planet, in general? I didn&#39;t see anything either way on the matter in the Exoplanets rulebook, except that it&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">says that if you upgrade a planet with at least 1 Life token on the beginning of your turn to a Species, you can skip placing any intermediate Life tokens and just replace the existing tokens with a Species.</span></p>",
